# Wildcard routes with variable number of parameters #699 - GitHub
created: 2011-06-06, last updated: 2025-10-18, [Read more](https://github.com/expressjs/express/issues/699)

From here, you will construct the string representing what the user defined route will be. This string will need to stored somewhere ( database / json object / whatever ). Something like,
```
...
```
...
Once you have defined the wildcard route in express, and defined the user-defined route as a strong somewhere else, you can simple parse the incoming
```
req.params[0]
```
using
```
route-parser
```
inside your express route handler.
Here is a psuedo example of what the handler would look like.
```
var myPath = `/:a/:b/:c`;
var Route = require('route-parser');
var route = new Route(myPath);
var routeParams = route.match("/" + req.params["0"]);
// if no route match is found, 404 with a friendly error
if (routeParams === false) {
res.writeHead(404);
res.end('Invalid path: ' + req.params["0"] + ' does not match ' + req.hook.path);
return;
}
// route matches, map route parameters to resource scope
for (var p in routeParams) {
req.params[p] = routeParams[p];
}
